Package: pretestsim
Type: Package
Title: Interactive Studio for the Pretest-Simulation Framework
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Benedict", "Kongyir", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "kongyirbenkk@gmail.com")
Description: A Shiny dashboard that drives the original, unmodified
    pretest-simulation framework ('user_framework_rpk_v3_0.R', bundled in
    'inst/framework') through the six phases of its run_simulation() engine:
    normality-test AUROC comparison, trade-off analysis and optimal-threshold
    selection, power vs Type I error ROC-like curves, power and Type I error
    across sample sizes (with AUC tables), and power vs effect size. The user
    chooses a classical or custom/ML normality assessment, supplies custom
    functions and optional trained-model RData, sets all simulation parameters
    (Nsim, N_tradeoff, tol_pos, loss_tol, effect_size, ...), and selects which
    phases to run.
